; emit-byte-throughput-100 --- raw 100-EMIT_BYTE_REG bytecode-size probe.
;
; Per §5.5 each EMIT_BYTE_REG is a single 32-bit instruction whose E
; stage iterates 9 SCL pulses (8 data bits from R7[7:0] MSB-first, then
; one ACK-slot pulse). The point of this probe is NOT runtime
; throughput (that's a hardware-sim question); it's to lock the
; BYTECODE size arithmetic for a 100-byte burst so any framing-overhead
; drift gets caught immediately.
;
; This is a controller-side fire-and-forget burst: every EMIT_BYTE_REG
; uses mask=0 (default), exempting it from the §5.5 ACK-pairing rule
; (E-WIRE-003). Per §5.5: "EMIT_BYTE_REG with mask=0 (fire-and-forget
; transmit, typical of probe traffic where ACK is intentionally
; ignored) is exempt from this requirement; no follow-up is required."
;
; Useful as a tripwire because the bytecode size is a closed-form
; function of the program shape and the §10 framing constants:
;
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Expected byte counts (computed from §5.5 + §10)
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; Body words:
;     LOAD_TIMING       1   (§5.17)
;     SET_BUS_MODE      1   (§5.13)
;     EMIT_BYTE_REG  x100   (§5.5; each is one 32-bit instruction)
;     HALT              1   (§5.10)
;     ------------------
;     total           103
;
; .molecode (raw SPRAM image: preamble + body, packed LE, no UART
; envelope; §10 "Program body" + §10 "Preamble (2 words = 8 bytes)"):
;
;     bytes = 2 preamble words × 4 + 103 body words × 4
;           =                   8 + 412
;           =                 420
;
; .mole.bin (UART frame; build_frame() in mole-asm/src/frame.rs:
; 2-byte LE length prefix + total_words × 4 bytes + 2-byte
; CRC-16/XMODEM trailer; total_words = preamble + body = 2 + 103 = 105):
;
;     bytes = 2 length + 105 total_words × 4 + 2 CRC
;           = 2        + 420                 + 2
;           = 424
;
; If a future change to §10 framing (e.g. adding a 4-byte session ID
; or a different CRC width) shifts either of these values by even one
; byte, the per-fixture byte-equality assertion in
; mole-asm/tests/golden.rs fires immediately. The two arithmetic
; equations above are the things to update in lock-step with the
; spec change.
;
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Why 100 (not 99 or 128)?
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; Round number, easy to eyeball in a hex dump, and small enough to
; stay well inside MAX_PROGRAM_WORDS = 8192. Not a magic number;
; "many sequential EMIT_BYTE_REG words at the canonical mask=0 default,
; with no ACK-pairing follow-ups" is the actual property being
; locked.

        LOAD_TIMING       reg=0, divider=59
        SET_BUS_MODE      i2c

        ; 100x EMIT_BYTE_REG (mask=0 default → fire-and-forget, exempt
        ; from §5.5 ACK-pairing rule). R7[7:0] is whatever it was
        ; at engine reset (per §8 register file the post-reset value
        ; is implementation-defined; this probe never sets R7 so the
        ; wire bits emitted are sim-only and not asserted here).
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
        EMIT_BYTE_REG
